From: 1DKT8H <szymonj159@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: ipa2-lite: re-enable AP filters after Q6 call setup

The modem-owned pipe-4 filter pointer observed on SDM660 points at a local
SRAM table whose body is never populated when ipa2-lite is used.  The AP
fallback already builds the 24 QMI-provided rules correctly and reapplies
their pointers after Q6 has finished configuring the data call.  However,
Q6 also clears IPA_FILTER, so restoring only the pointers still leaves the
filter engine bypassed and every packet falls through to route index 7.

Keep using the AP-owned fallback until the missing uC programming path is
implemented.  Re-enable filtering only after both v4 and v6 pointers have
been committed through the command pipe, immediately before releasing the
filter lock.  This matches the ordering required by the hardware and avoids
exposing a partially updated table.

Signed-off-by: 1DKT8H <szymonj159@gmail.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm630.dtsi | 1 -
 drivers/net/ipa2-lite/ipa.c           | 2 ++
 2 files changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm630.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm630.dtsi
index b459390..564bbb0 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm630.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm630.dtsi
@@ -1040,6 +1040,5 @@
 		ipa: ipa@14780000 {
 			compatible = "qcom,ipa-lite-v2.6";
-			qcom,modem-cfg-emb-pipe-flt;
 			reg = <0x14780000 0x47000>;
 			clocks = <&rpmcc RPM_SMD_IPA_CLK>;
 			interrupts = <GIC_SPI 333 IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_RISING>,
diff --git a/drivers/net/ipa2-lite/ipa.c b/drivers/net/ipa2-lite/ipa.c
index c1192a0..c3c8d61 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ipa2-lite/ipa.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ipa2-lite/ipa.c
@@ -705,6 +705,8 @@ static int ipa_filter_reapply(struct ipa *ipa)
 	ret = ipa_filter_update_pointer(ipa, MEM_FT_V4, v4_addr);
 	if (!ret)
 		ret = ipa_filter_update_pointer(ipa, MEM_FT_V6, v6_addr);
+	if (!ret)
+		iowrite32(1, ipa->mmio + REG_IPA_FILTER_OFST);
 	mutex_unlock(&ipa->filter_lock);
 
 	return ret;
-- 
2.51.0
